= Open Source Fonts Guide

This document summarizes selected open source fonts for programming and technical writing.

 Open Source Fonts Guide

 1. Microsoft Cascadia Code
Repository: `https://github.com/microsoft/cascadia-code`

Cascadia Code is Microsoft's modern programming font family. It was designed for terminals, editors and development environments. It includes programming ligatures and a companion font Cascadia Mono without ligatures.

- Type: Monospace, sans-serif
- License: SIL Open Font License
- Best for: VS Code, Windows Terminal, PowerShell, C and general programming
- Features: OpenType ligatures, variable fonts, extensive symbols
- Notes: Cascadia Mono is recommended when strict character alignment is preferred.

 2. Ubuntu Sans Mono
Repository: `https://github.com/canonical/Ubuntu-Sans-Mono-fonts`

Ubuntu Sans Mono is Canonical's modern Ubuntu system font family. It replaces older Ubuntu Mono with improved readability and broader Unicode support.

- Type: Monospace, sans-serif
- License: Ubuntu Font License
- Best for: Linux terminals, programming, documentation
- Notes: Cleaner and more modern than Ubuntu Mono.

 3. DejaVu Fonts
Repository: `https://github.com/dejavu-fonts/dejavu-fonts`

DejaVu provides a very broad Unicode coverage based on Bitstream Vera. DejaVu Sans Mono is one of the most common Linux monospace fonts.

- Type: Sans, serif and monospace families
- License: Bitstream Vera License
- Best for: Linux desktop, terminals, fallback font
- Notes: Excellent compatibility, but visual style is older.

 4. Fira Code
Repository: `https://github.com/tonsky/FiraCode`

Fira Code is one of the most popular programming fonts. It extends Fira Mono with programming ligatures.

- Type: Monospace
- License: SIL Open Font License
- Best for: Modern IDEs
- Features: Ligatures such as arrows and operators
- Notes: Excellent coding readability.

 5. JetBrains Mono
Repository: `https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono`

JetBrains Mono was designed specifically for software developers.

- Type: Monospace
- License: SIL Open Font License
- Features: Large x-height, distinctive symbols, ligatures
- Best for: Long programming sessions
- Notes: One of the strongest general-purpose coding fonts.

 6. IBM Plex
Repository: `https://github.com/IBM/plex`

IBM Plex is IBM's corporate typeface family.

- Type: Sans, serif and mono
- License: SIL Open Font License
- Best for: UI, technical documents, programming
- Notes: IBM Plex Mono is a high-quality professional monospace font.

 7. Noto CJK
Repository: `https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk`

Noto CJK is Google's large-scale Unicode CJK font project.

- Type: Sans and serif
- License: SIL Open Font License
- Best for: Chinese/Japanese/Korean text
- Notes: Excellent CJK coverage and recommended for Unicode fallback.

 8. Sarasa Gothic
Repository: `https://github.com/be5invis/Sarasa-Gothic`

Sarasa Gothic combines Iosevka with Source Han Sans to create a CJK programming font family.

- Type: Monospace and proportional variants
- License: SIL Open Font License
- Best for: Chinese programming environments
- Features: CJK glyphs aligned with Latin monospace characters
- Notes: One of the best choices for mixed Chinese comments and code.

 9. Sarasa Term SC Nerd
Repository: `https://github.com/laishulu/Sarasa-Term-SC-Nerd`

A Nerd Fonts patched version of Sarasa Term SC.

- Type: Monospace CJK programming font
- Features: Nerd Font icons
- Best for: Terminal, Neovim, VS Code
- Notes: Good for modern terminal workflows.

 10. Maple Font
Repository: `https://github.com/subframe7536/maple-font`

Maple is a modern Chinese programming font family.

- Type: Monospace with CJK support
- Features: Programming ligatures, modern glyph design
- Best for: Coding and Chinese comments
- Notes: Attractive modern alternative to older CJK fonts.

 11. LXGW WenKai
Repository: `https://github.com/lxgw/LxgwWenKai`

LXGW WenKai is an open-source Chinese handwriting-style font.

- Type: Proportional serif-like Chinese font
- License: SIL Open Font License
- Best for: Reading, notes, documents
- Notes: Not a coding monospace font, but excellent for Chinese text.

 Recommendations

For programming:
1. JetBrains Mono
2. Cascadia Code / Cascadia Mono
3. Sarasa Term SC Nerd
4. Maple Mono

For Chinese code comments:
1. Sarasa Gothic
2. Maple
3. Noto Sans CJK

For documents:
1. IBM Plex
2. LXGW WenKai
3. Noto Serif CJK
